-- title:
--   A supported divisor term inherits the canonical boundary estimate
-- statement:
--   Let $\chi$ be a smooth sieve cutoff, $k\ge2$, $N\ne0$, and $R,W,b\in\mathbb N$. For a selected CFZ pattern $e$ with $m$ forms and $2R^{2m}\le N$, choose a supported divisor family $z$. The absolute difference between its coefficient-weighted divisibility density and coefficient-weighted canonical carry Euler average is at most $|c_z|C_e\operatorname{pairedDivisorLcm}(z)/N$, where $c_z$ is its smooth coefficient and $C_e$ is the selected canonical cyclic boundary constant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/GreenTao/Sieve/CFZCanonicalCyclicBoundaryLimit.lean#L43-L129

